WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.629
If you want to my theory on why Chucky willingly
decided to mutilate himself towards the end of

00:00:04.629 --> 00:00:07.180
the movie then stick around to the end of
this video.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:15.680
Welcome back to Things You Missed, in the
last episode I covered the original Child’s

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.759
Play -- you can check that out here if you
want -- so this time let’s reopen the toybox

00:00:19.759 --> 00:00:21.949
and take a stab at Child’s Play 2.

00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:25.490
This one opens up by showing the aftermath
that the events of the first movie had on

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:29.590
the company that makes the Good Guy dolls:
Play Pal Toys, and their boss, Mr. Sullivan.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:34.360
As the President of a major toy company, Mr.
Sullivan has a custom license plate that says:

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.360
“FUN ONE”.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.630
The other executive is later shown to have
license plate “EXEC 4”.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.540
We will see more of Mr. Sullivan and a little
bit about why he’s known as The Fun One

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.340
in the next sequel, but in this movie, he’s
not in the mood for fun and games.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:51.640
You know, ‘hi, I’m Chucky, I’m the Lakeshore
Strangler and I’m gonna kill you’....

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.560
Well, something like that.”

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:59.170
The opening title this time takes on a new
look as compared to the previous movie, this

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:03.050
time it looks a lot like the font seen the
badges that the employees of Play Pal Toys

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.050
wear.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.390
The Chucky doll from the last movie is cleaned
up and restored using a variety of instruments,

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.390
including actual dental tools, which reminds
me of that one guy from Toy Story 2, who is

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:13.340
apparently big with the ASMR community.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.180
“The part where he paints woody's shoe with
the paint brush.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.190
Oooooofff.”

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.200
“And I thought I was the only one satisfied
by this scene…”

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:28.310
“this is my favorite scene from Toy Story
2, it's so aesthetically pleasing omgahhhh”

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:33.030
OK, enough of that, but this one of the many
connections between the two franchises -- such

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.280
as the protagonist being a kid named Andy
and the 2019 installments sharing a release

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.659
date on June 21st.

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:41.940
The new Child’s Play even has a poster that's mocking
is Pixar counterpart.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.640
So Chucky’s body is restored.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.619
I don’t really know why they felt the need
to fix up THIS particular doll -- they could

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:51.159
have just produced a new doll named Chucky
and shown that to their stockholders instead.

00:01:51.159 --> 00:01:52.620
It would have been a lot less work.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.510
But no, had to go with the cursed one, and
of course, things go wrong.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.420
[electrocution clip]

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:02.320
“Ah **** here we go again.”

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.700
We are then reintroduced to Andy Barclay,
who is now at a foster home after his mom

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.280
was put away in the looney bin.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.240
Andy has a bad dream about Chucky.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.760
“You know dreams can’t hurt ya.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.170
Dreams aren’t real, right?”

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:19.000
Apparently this guy has never seen A Nightmare
on Elm Street.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.280
Andy ends up getting adopted by The Simpsons.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.510
No, not those Simpsons, we’ll save them
for my Treehouse of Horror episodes of Things

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:26.510
You Missed.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:30.040
THESE Simpsons are known for taking many foster
children over the years, and their walls are

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:34.650
painted in baby blue and pink -- the colors
commonly associated with a nursery -- to reflect

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.650
that.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:36.960
Andy takes a look around the house.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:37.840
"You like it?"

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:38.580
"Uh-huh."

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.940
“It’s been in my family for three generations.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.290
My grandmother gave it to my mother and my
mother gave it to me.”

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.420
“And who are you gonna give it to?”

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.500
Daaannngggg this kid just lit her on FIRE!

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.610
It would not be long before she got her revenge
though.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.980
“I made those curtains just for you.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.720
I bet blue is your favorite color.”

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.520
So let me get this straight.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:05.270
You made the curtains specifically for Andy,
and yet you left a Good Guy doll in the closet,

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.100
knowing full well he has PTSD with Good Guy
dolls?

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.520
I mean what the hell is that?

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.099
Also found in the closet, is this skateboard
known as the Nash Nightmare Board from the

00:03:13.099 --> 00:03:14.099
80s.

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:17.910
It’s decorated with a character that looks
like Jason from Friday the 13th, and the name

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:21.590
Nightmare Board is a bit of a nod to Freddy
Krueger’s franchise that I mentioned a minute

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.090
ago -- A Nightmare on Elm Street.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:26.160
The other faces on the board just seem to
be generic horror characters.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.940
That night, Chucky tries to get more information
about Andy Barclay’s location and he calls

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:30.940
the foster home.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.480
A little boy named Sammy asks the caretaker
to play a game called “red light.”

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.760
“I wanna play Red Light.”

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.760
“No Sammy, I don’t want to play Red Light
now I want you to back to bed right now.”

00:03:39.770 --> 00:03:42.990
This is one of many references to traffic
lights in this movie.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.080
Andy has a shirt with traffic lights on it
and there seems to be an emphasis on them

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.080
in some of the shots.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.800
I’m not 100% sure on what the meaning of
these are -- perhaps just a hint that Chucky

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.700
will be riding in vehicles during the climax
of this movie.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:58.129
Also, the blood-red phone that connects Chucky
and the foster home lady could be a clue about

00:03:58.129 --> 00:03:59.129
later.

00:03:59.129 --> 00:04:02.770
Andy’s new foster mother reads him Hansel
and Gretel as a bedtime story, but she gets

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:06.720
West Dakota level lazy and just kind of skips
to the happily ever after part.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.180
“...and they all live happily ever after.”

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.840
“No they don’t!”

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:13.620
“They do for now, we’ll finish it tomorrow
night.”

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:18.120
I almost wonder if this is kind of a clue
that maybe at the time Child’s Play 2 was

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.709
made, it was supposed to be a trilogy.

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:23.750
We get our happily ever after at the end of
2 -- but in reality, we finish things up in

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.590
three where Chucky is finished off once and
for all.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:30.440
We now know that that doesn’t happen, but
it does still hold true to this era of Child’s

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.370
Play movies being a set of three.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.910
After Child’s Play 3, the series totally
shifts towards full-comedy, and the movies

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.250
take on a different naming scheme.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:41.090
I think a lot of people see the first three
as a set -- then Bride and Seed as a set,

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.460
and finally Curse and Cult as a third era.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:47.340
When Chucky buries the other Good Guy doll
known as Tommy, he uses a Toy Shovel, which

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.800
is in line with the Good Guy accessories seen
being sold in the first movie.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.750
Play Pal Toys unknowingly gave Chucky a whole
arsenal of weapons it seems.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:58.530
Andy’s new parents are concerned by his
behaviour and have a discussion about him

00:04:58.530 --> 00:04:59.530
in the kitchen.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.810
OK, seriously, how do they not hear him eavesdropping
right here?

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:05.750
This episode is already turning into Shaggy
Questions The Logic of Horror Movies Part

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:06.240
II.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:08.280
And honestly, you guys are here for it aren’t
you?

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.919
Alright let’s try to move on.

00:05:09.919 --> 00:05:11.060
OH WOW.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.060
OK.

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.520
This would be a realllllyyyy bad look in 2019.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.530
Let’s actually skip ahead a little further
to……

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.030
Andy going on the school bus.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:21.280
There should actually be some Things You Missed
in this scene.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:24.690
So Andy gets on the bus and several kids are
wearing Good Guys merchandise.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.620
And this one kid is extremely hostile!

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.760
Wow, what did Andy do to you dude?

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.320
Somebody call Jake Paul, we’ve got a cyberbully.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.070
Or actually just a regular bully I guess.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.790
Andy’s teacher, Mrs. Kettlewell reads a
story to the class.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:45.259
She’s reading Pinocchio, the tale of a puppet
who is turned into a real boy, a clear parallel

00:05:45.259 --> 00:05:49.020
to Chucky being a toy who is turned into a
real human at the end of the movie.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:52.240
Chucky sabotages Andy’s schoolwork, earning
him a detention after school.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.229
Are you kidding me, the teacher locks him
in there?

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:55.300
What if there’s a fire?

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.020
What if there’s a gas leak and he needs
to get out?

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:02.130
Yeah, not the best idea -- so when Chucky
kills her with a ball pump (if you were wondering

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:04.450
what that was) she almost kind of deserves
it.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:08.139
Andy is able to get home safely though, and
Mr. Simpson is getting fed up with the stories

00:06:08.139 --> 00:06:09.270
about Chucky.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.140
“Open the door.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.100
OPEN IT!

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.120
OPEN IT!

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.600
“Hey V-Sauce, Michael here.”

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:29.590
Andy gets the meat carver that night and decides
to take matters into his own hands, but Phil

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:34.000
hears the commotion and comes down to investigate,
unfortunately becoming the next victim of

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.000
Chucky.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.471
The woman from the foster home has to come
and pick up Andy and Kyle, as they’ll no

00:06:37.471 --> 00:06:39.240
longer be able to stay in this home.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:42.320
As she’s explaining things to him, there’s
a carousel in the background.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.900
This is probably just a random set piece to
go along with the clowns seen in the upstairs

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:50.180
bedroom, but the analytical side of my brain
likes to see this as a symbol for Andy’s

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.800
current state of life, how he’s constantly
being thrown back into this loop that just

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:58.050
goes around and around in cycles of being
assigned to a new home, getting attacked by

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.940
Chucky, getting sent back to the nursing home
and then getting assigned to yet another new

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:07.639
home; never escaping the danger and constantly
going around and around like a Merry-Go-Round.

00:07:07.639 --> 00:07:11.120
But then I remember, it’s a movie about
a killer children’s toy and probably doesn’t

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.330
go that deep.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:16.389
Kyle discovers the other Good Guy doll that
Chucky buried earlier, but gets ambushed by

00:07:16.389 --> 00:07:17.940
him before she can do anything.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:21.289
He forces her to drive to the foster home,
but they get pulled over on the way.

00:07:21.289 --> 00:07:24.670
Lucky for her, he’s a fan of Good Guy dolls
I guess…?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.400
And he asks what the doll’s name is.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.940
“Chucky.”

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:29.760
*laughter*

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.600
Hold up, how would the cop not realize something
was up here?

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:36.440
I mean they’ve already established that the events
of the first movie were all over the news.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:40.310
And I imagine the company would not continue
to name any dolls “Chucky” after their

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:41.310
little PR disaster.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:44.980
Well, anyways, he doesn’t seem to notice
anything is up, and Chucky makes it to the

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:49.009
foster home, where he pulls the fire alarm
to try to smoke out Andy as quickly as possible.

00:07:49.009 --> 00:07:52.229
The kids file out, and I noticed many of them
are wearing Good Guys shirts.

00:07:52.229 --> 00:07:56.520
Again, you’d think they might be encouraged
NOT to wear those because of the whole Andy

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.830
PTSD thing.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:58.840
Seems a little bit rude.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:02.650
Also, one of the kids had on a Bon Jovi shirt
-- which I just now noticed and coincidentally

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:05.930
has nothing to do with the fact that I said
Bon Jovi would have made a perfect closing

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:09.510
track during the Things You Missed episode
for the first movie even though they didn’t

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:10.510
put it in.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:14.509
Swear I didn’t plan this, I literally just
noticed the Bon Jovi shirt during this video.

00:08:14.509 --> 00:08:17.259
So Andy freezes on the stairs when he spots
Chucky.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:21.360
Not sure why he didn’t just stay with the
group, it probably would have been a lot safer since Chucky

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.780
doesn’t like to reveal himself as a living
doll, but as we know, Andy isn’t the smartest

00:08:25.789 --> 00:08:26.789
kid either.

00:08:26.789 --> 00:08:29.180
So Chucky kills that lady and escapes with
Andy.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:34.320
Whatever kid drew this dinosaur was obviously very
confused, this is clearly not a T-Rex…

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.980
Actually it was probably Andy who drew that.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:40.440
Now there’s one part in the newspaper truck
here that I need to pause at, not to explain

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:45.380
a Thing You Missed, but rather so I can say
DAAAAA BEARS.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:49.200
So Kyle is chasing Chucky and Andy,
because this movie has character arcs and

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:51.920
I guess she actually cares about the little
snot head now.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:56.139
She runs the truck driver off the road and
it just happens to be right near the factory,

00:08:56.139 --> 00:08:59.480
so one obvious Indiana Jones reference later,
we’re inside the factory.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:02.100
This is actually the best part of the movie,
so pay attention.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:06.089
Chucky does the voodoo spell on Andy once
again, causing the storm clouds to roll in.

00:09:06.089 --> 00:09:09.619
Tom Skilling must have been losing his g*******
mind during these movies.

00:09:09.619 --> 00:09:13.460
The spell doesn’t work because Chucky was
too late, he’s already become human, so

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.310
he goes for the next best thing: revenge.

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:17.300
“Some BODY”.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:20.699
Ok, but actually right here we get a better
look at the box, and it’s the same mistake

00:09:20.699 --> 00:09:23.939
from the last movie where it says Play Partners
Toys instead of Play Pals.

00:09:23.939 --> 00:09:28.110
We also get a better look at the side of the
box which notes that batteries are included.

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:31.889
The working title for the original Child’s
Play was “Batteries Not Included”, but

00:09:31.889 --> 00:09:34.730
then I guess they decided they wanted the
batteries to be included for that whole plot

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:38.350
point about Andy’s Mom realizing that Chucky
was operating without the batteries, so they

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:40.790
changed it, and added this to the box.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:44.600
As Andy and Kyle run away, I noticed this
box is already ripped, but they haven’t

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:45.699
even done anything over here yet.

00:09:45.699 --> 00:09:48.540
Talk about bad quality control Play Pal Toys.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:52.679
Andy and Kyle flee up this ramp, and Chuckers
gets the old arm trapped under this gate.

00:09:52.679 --> 00:09:56.499
Not sure why he doesn’t just open the gate,
he’s shown some strength in the past and

00:09:56.499 --> 00:09:58.980
it really doesn’t look that heavy, but he
decides, ‘you know what?

00:09:58.980 --> 00:09:59.999
I’m pulling my arm off.’

00:09:59.999 --> 00:10:02.800
Maybe he really wanted to have a knife for
an arm and he did it on purpose.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:06.379
Like ever since he was 7 and he realized his
punches don’t do that much damage, he just

00:10:06.379 --> 00:10:09.910
decided right then and there: ‘When I grow
up, I’m gonna have a knife for an arm, and

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:11.920
there’s nothing you can do about it Mom!’

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:16.489
So then we get to this machine, which apparently
produces mangled up monster toys, and they

00:10:16.489 --> 00:10:19.929
staple Chucky down to it and he seemingly
dies.

00:10:19.929 --> 00:10:24.389
Except this is a Child’s Play movie, and
like the previous one, he comes back.

00:10:24.389 --> 00:10:25.949
So they melt him alive.

00:10:25.949 --> 00:10:26.949
And he comes back.

00:10:26.949 --> 00:10:29.720
So this time they blow up his head, and I
guess that works.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:32.470
It just ends pretty abruptly.

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:35.721
Much like this video, if you want to see the
Things You Missed in the next movie, that

00:10:35.721 --> 00:10:38.939
video will be on the left once the video comes
out later this week.

00:10:38.939 --> 00:10:43.259
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring the deathbell for

00:10:43.259 --> 00:10:46.259
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:48.820
Assuming we both survive.

